  n<//-------------------------------------------------------> u<282> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<5045> s<283> f<1> l<141:1> el<141:58>
  n<// Input synchronizers> u<283> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<5045> s<284> f<1> l<142:1> el<142:23>
  n<//-------------------------------------------------------> u<284> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<5045> s<285> f<1> l<143:1> el<143:58>
  n<// In some cases, the asynchronous input ports might> u<285> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<5045> s<286> f<1> l<144:1> el<144:53>
  n<// already be synchronized externally.> u<286> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<5045> s<287> f<1> l<145:1> el<145:39>
  n<// If an extensive CDC design review showed that this> u<287> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<5045> s<288> f<1> l<146:1> el<146:54>
  n<// is really the case,  the individual synchronizers> u<288> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<5045> s<289> f<1> l<147:1> el<147:53>
  n<// can be disabled with the following defines.> u<289> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<5045> s<290> f<1> l<148:1> el<148:47>
  n<//> u<290> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<5045> s<291> f<1> l<149:1> el<149:3>
