  n<//        - Possibility to generate a software PUC reset> u<277> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<278> f<1> l<130:1> el<130:57>
  n<//-------------------------------------------------------> u<278> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<279> f<1> l<131:1> el<131:58>
  n<//-------------------------------------------------------> u<279> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<280> f<1> l<135:1> el<135:58>
  n<// Include/Exclude Non-Maskable-Interrupt support> u<280> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<281> f<1> l<136:1> el<136:50>
  n<//-------------------------------------------------------> u<281> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<282> f<1> l<137:1> el<137:58>
  n<//-------------------------------------------------------> u<282> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<283> f<1> l<141:1> el<141:58>
  n<// Input synchronizers> u<283> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<284> f<1> l<142:1> el<142:23>
  n<//-------------------------------------------------------> u<284> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<285> f<1> l<143:1> el<143:58>
  n<// In some cases, the asynchronous input ports might> u<285> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<286> f<1> l<144:1> el<144:53>
  n<// already be synchronized externally.> u<286> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<287> f<1> l<145:1> el<145:39>
  n<// If an extensive CDC design review showed that this> u<287> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<288> f<1> l<146:1> el<146:54>
  n<// is really the case,  the individual synchronizers> u<288> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<289> f<1> l<147:1> el<147:53>
  n<// can be disabled with the following defines.> u<289> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<290> f<1> l<148:1> el<148:47>
  n<//> u<290> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<291> f<1> l<149:1> el<149:3>
  n<// Notes:> u<291> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<292> f<1> l<150:1> el<150:10>
  n<//        - all three signals are all sampled in the MCLK domain> u<292> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<293> f<1> l<151:1> el<151:65>
  n<//> u<293> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<294> f<1> l<152:1> el<152:3>
  n<//        - the dbg_en signal reset the debug interface> u<294> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<295> f<1> l<153:1> el<153:56>
  n<//         when 0. Therefore make sure it is glitch free.> u<295> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<296> f<1> l<154:1> el<154:58>
  n<//> u<296> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<297> f<1> l<155:1> el<155:3>
  n<//-------------------------------------------------------> u<297> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<298> f<1> l<156:1> el<156:58>
  n<//`define SYNC_CPU_EN> u<298> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<299> f<1> l<158:1> el<158:22>
  n<//`define SYNC_DBG_EN> u<299> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<300> f<1> l<159:1> el<159:22>
  n<//-------------------------------------------------------> u<300> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<301> f<1> l<162:1> el<162:58>
  n<// Peripheral Memory Space:> u<301> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<302> f<1> l<163:1> el<163:28>
  n<//-------------------------------------------------------> u<302> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<303> f<1> l<164:1> el<164:58>
  n<// The original MSP430 architecture map the peripherals> u<303> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<304> f<1> l<165:1> el<165:56>
  n<// from 0x0000 to 0x01FF (i.e. 512B of the memory space).> u<304> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<305> f<1> l<166:1> el<166:58>
  n<// The following defines allow you to expand this space> u<305> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<306> f<1> l<167:1> el<167:56>
  n<// up to 32 kB (i.e. from 0x0000 to 0x7fff).> u<306> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<307> f<1> l<168:1> el<168:45>
  n<// As a consequence, the data memory mapping will be> u<307> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<308> f<1> l<169:1> el<169:53>
  n<// shifted up and a custom linker script will therefore> u<308> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<309> f<1> l<170:1> el<170:56>
  n<// be required by the GCC compiler.> u<309> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<310> f<1> l<171:1> el<171:36>
  n<//-------------------------------------------------------> u<310> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<10007> s<311> f<1> l<172:1> el<172:58>
