  n<//-------------------------------------------------------> u<279> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<3472> s<280> f<1> l<131:1> el<131:58>
  n<//-------------------------------------------------------> u<280> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<3472> s<281> f<1> l<135:1> el<135:58>
  n<// Include/Exclude Non-Maskable-Interrupt support> u<281> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<3472> s<282> f<1> l<136:1> el<136:50>
  n<//-------------------------------------------------------> u<282> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<3472> s<283> f<1> l<137:1> el<137:58>
  n<//-------------------------------------------------------> u<283> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<3472> s<284> f<1> l<141:1> el<141:58>
  n<// Input synchronizers> u<284> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<3472> s<285> f<1> l<142:1> el<142:23>
  n<//-------------------------------------------------------> u<285> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<3472> s<286> f<1> l<143:1> el<143:58>
  n<// In some cases, the asynchronous input ports might> u<286> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<3472> s<287> f<1> l<144:1> el<144:53>
  n<// already be synchronized externally.> u<287> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<3472> s<288> f<1> l<145:1> el<145:39>
  n<// If an extensive CDC design review showed that this> u<288> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<3472> s<289> f<1> l<146:1> el<146:54>
  n<// is really the case,  the individual synchronizers> u<289> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<3472> s<290> f<1> l<147:1> el<147:53>
  n<// can be disabled with the following defines.> u<290> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<3472> s<291> f<1> l<148:1> el<148:47>
  n<//> u<291> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<3472> s<292> f<1> l<149:1> el<149:3>
  n<// Notes:> u<292> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<3472> s<293> f<1> l<150:1> el<150:10>
